><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="9" rect="595.276001,269.083618,779.276001,361.083618"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251029143644+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="3de4c1da-7a20-4aa6-9a80-3f6fea7fe31e" date="D:20251029143644+10'00'" name="4a25b8fd-0a37-4bc1-be2c-7828eec3cbe0" icon="Comment" page="9" rect="62.056564,337.389252,86.056564,361.389252" subject="Sticky Note" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>The IMUs had very good reliability between trials&#xD;when assessing impact loading of gymnastics skills.&#xD;Signal analysis procedures should be considered when&#xD;interpreting reliability results, as optimally filtered&#xD;acceleration data showed improved reliability compared&#xD;to the raw signal. Also, distal-mounted IMUs&#xD;demonstrated higher levels of reliability (forearm and&#xD;tibia positions) compared to upper and lower back&#xD;positions. It is therefore suggested that forearmmounted&#xD;IMUs and tibia-mounted IMUs be utilised&#xD;when assessing upper limb and lower limb impacts&#xD;when performing gymnastics skills, respectively.&#xD;Therefore, IMUs can be used to monitor limb loading&#xD;of young gymnasts and provide insight into the relationship&#xD;between training load and injury in artistic&#xD;gymnastics. This information would be extremely beneficial&#xD;for coaches and support personal (i.e. physiotherapists),&#xD;to assist with designing training schedules&#xD;and rehabilitation programs that could potentially&#xD;reduce overuse injury risk in artistic gymnastics.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="9" rect="595.276001,269.389252,779.276001,361.389252"
